# Multi-Page Static Site (MPA) Philosophy

Organize the project as a static multi-page app (MPA). Each major feature or section should have its own HTML file, with shared CSS and JS included via <link> and <script> tags. Avoid deep nesting; keep the structure flat and easy to navigate. Use web components and Shoelace for UI, and ensure all pages are accessible and mobile-friendly.

## Guidelines
- Each main feature (e.g., activities, calendar, memories) should have a dedicated HTML file (e.g., [activities.html](mdc:activities.html)).
- Shared styles and scripts should be placed in [css/styles.css](mdc:css/styles.css) and [js/] directory files, and included on each page.
- Do not use client-side routing or SPA frameworks; navigation is handled by standard links between HTML files.
- Keep the directory structure flat and simple, with minimal subfolders.
- All pages must be mobile-first and accessible, leveraging Shoelace and native HTML elements.
- No build tools or bundlers; all files must be directly usable in the browser.
